    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nUI2 currently collapses messages exceeding the `cmd` target’s available height and replaces subsequent output with a `[+n]` spill indicator. This prevents newly arriving messages from remaining visible, and makes it hard to see when a command or task has finished.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMaybe an option for the `cmd` target to instead:\n\n1. Scroll older messages out of view.\n2. Continue displaying incoming messages.\n3. Show an indicator containing the number of older hidden lines, e.g. `[10+]`.\n\nPerhaps a configuration such as this:\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({\n  msg = {\n    cmd = {\n      overflow = \"scroll\",\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe current behavior could remain the default under `overflow = \"collapse\"`.",
